# hw definition for a custom TBS Lucid H7 OEM variant that adds a hardware
# ToneAlarm (pitched-tone) buzzer on the "S13/LED" pad.
#
# The stock buzzer output (PA15) is a plain GPIO; its only timer channel,
# TIM2_CH1, is already taken by motor output 1, so ArduPilot tunes only
# come out as single-pitch on/off beeps. This variant repurposes the
# WS2812 LED pad - PA8, servo output 13 - as a hardware tone output: PA8
# is marked ALARM on TIM1_CH1, which defines HAL_PWM_ALARM so AP_ToneAlarm
# plays the full pitched tunes on a passive buzzer wired to S13/LED. TIM1
# drives nothing else on this board (outputs 1-12 use TIM2/3/4/5/15, the
# system timer is TIM12).
#
# Cost: the addressable LED-strip output (servo output 13). Outputs 1-12
# are unchanged. The onboard PA15 buzzer output stays; set NTF_BUZZ_PIN -1
# to silence an active buzzer on it.
#
# Board ID is inherited (AP_HW_TBS_LUCID_H7_OEM), so the .apj flashes over
# the stock bootloader as a normal firmware update. See Readme.md.

include ../TBS_LUCID_H7_OEM/hwdef.dat

undef PA8
PA8 TIM1_CH1 TIM1 GPIO(62) ALARM
